From: PB624 bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: sun5i: PE1 can be a GPIO output

The A13 pin table lists PE0-PE2 as input only, but the PocketBook 624
drives the e-ink VDD rail from PE1 (function 1 = output, as on PE3+).

---
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun5i.c	2026-10-10 21:37:37.498016200 +0300
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun5i.c	2026-10-10 21:37:37.502016340 +0300
@@ -527,6 +527,7 @@
 		  SUNXI_FUNCTION_IRQ(0x6, 14)),		/* EINT14 */
 	SUNXI_PIN(SUNXI_PINCTRL_PIN(E, 1),
 		  SUNXI_FUNCTION(0x0, "gpio_in"),
+		  SUNXI_FUNCTION(0x1, "gpio_out"),
 		  SUNXI_FUNCTION(0x2, "ts0"),		/* ERR */
 		  SUNXI_FUNCTION(0x3, "csi0"),		/* CK */
 		  SUNXI_FUNCTION(0x4, "spi2"),		/* CLK */
